{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FlatTetrahedra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTetrahedra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.edge_equations_do_not_detect_hyperbolicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.edge_equations_do_not_detect_hyperbolicity","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L245-L256","doc":"**The headline, stated as one theorem: the edge equations do not detect\nhyperbolicity.**\n\nThe trefoil complement is Seifert fibred, not hyperbolic, yet its shapes satisfy the edge\nequations and have volume `0`.  So satisfying the gluing equations is *not* sufficient for\na geometric solution — positivity of the imaginary parts is the missing condition, and it\nis exactly what `IdealTetrahedron.im_pos` supplies. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:gluing-equations-do-not-detect-hyperbolicity","label":"thm:gluing-equations-do-not-detect-hyperbolicity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gluing-equations-do-not-detect-hyperbolicity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_volume_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_volume_zero","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L241-L243","doc":"**The trefoil triangulation has volume zero** — every tetrahedron is flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_flat","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L235-L239","doc":"Both trefoil shapes are flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_edge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_edge_one","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L229-L233","doc":"**Trefoil edge equation 1**, exponents `[1,0,0, 0,1,0]`: `z₀ · z₁′ = (−1)(−1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_edge_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoil_edge_zero","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L219-L227","doc":"**Trefoil edge equation 0**, exponents `[1,2,2, 2,1,2]`:\n`z₀ · (z₀′)² · (z₀″)² · (z₁)² · z₁′ · (z₁″)² = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoilTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoilTriangulation","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L215-L217","doc":"The trefoil's two-tetrahedron shape data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoilShape₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoilShape₁","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L211-L213","doc":"The trefoil's second shape, `z₁ = 2`.  **Rational**, hence flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoilShape₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.trefoilShape₀","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L207-L209","doc":"The trefoil's first shape, `z₀ = −1`.  **Rational**, hence flat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.volume_eq_zero_of_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.volume_eq_zero_of_flat","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L195-L199","doc":"**If every shape is flat the total volume is zero.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.volume","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L191-L193","doc":"Total volume — well defined with flat shapes present, which contribute `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.SatisfiesEdgeEquations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.SatisfiesEdgeEquations","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L185-L189","doc":"**The edge gluing equations**, stated over possibly-flat shapes.  Same formula as\n`MathlibExt.SatisfiesEdgeEquations`, without the positivity requirement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.tet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.tet","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L181-L181","doc":"The shapes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L179-L179","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.ShapedTriangulation","kind":"structure","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L178-L181","doc":"A collection of `n` shapes, flat ones allowed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.toShape_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.toShape_param","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L170-L174","doc":"The two `param`s agree, so nothing proved about `IdealTetrahedron.param` is lost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.toShape_z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.toShape_z","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L168-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.toShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.toShape","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L161-L166","doc":"Every `IdealTetrahedron` is a `Shape` — the positivity requirement is dropped, not\ncontradicted, so all existing results remain available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.volume_eq_zero_of_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.volume_eq_zero_of_flat","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L155-L157","doc":"**A flat shape has zero volume.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.IsFlat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.IsFlat","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L152-L153","doc":"A shape is **flat** when it is real — the degenerate tetrahedron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.volume","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L149-L150","doc":"The volume contributed by this shape.  Defined for flat shapes too, where it is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_prod","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L141-L147","doc":"**`z · z′ · z″ = −1`** — pure algebra, no positivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L125-L139","doc":"**Every edge parameter is nonzero** — from `z ≠ 0, 1` alone.\n\n`IdealTriangulation.param_ne_zero` proves the same thing from `param_im_pos`, i.e. from\npositivity.  Positivity is not what makes the parameters units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_two","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_one","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L122-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L121-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.param","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The three edge parameters, same convention as `IdealTetrahedron.param`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.one_sub_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.one_sub_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L107-L107","doc":"Excluded so `1/(1−z)` is a genuine unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Excluded so the edge parameters are genuine units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.z","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The shape parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.Shape","kind":"structure","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L99-L107","doc":"A **shape parameter**: any `z ∈ ℂ ∖ {0,1}`.  Unlike `IdealTetrahedron` this does\n**not** require `0 < Im z`, so flat (real) shapes are permitted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.BlochWigner_lob_eq_zero_of_im_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.BlochWigner_lob_eq_zero_of_im_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**Flat ⇒ zero volume**, in the form the geometry layer wants: a shape with vanishing\nimaginary part contributes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.BlochWigner_lob_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.BlochWigner_lob_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L70-L83","doc":"**A real shape parameter gives zero volume — unconditionally.**\n\nGeneralises `BlochWigner_lob_real_eq_zero`, which assumed `0 < x < 1`.  No hypothesis is\nneeded, and that includes the two junk-value cases: at `x = 1` Lean's `1/0 = 0` makes\n`1/(1−x) = 0`, and at `x = 0` it makes `1 − 1/x = 1`; both give `arg = 0`, so the formula\nstill returns `0`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:flat-tetrahedron-zero-volume","label":"thm:flat-tetrahedron-zero-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/flat-tetrahedron-zero-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FlatTet.arg_ofReal_zero_or_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FlatTet.arg_ofReal_zero_or_pi","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FlatTetrahedra.lean#L62-L68","doc":"The argument of a real number is `0` or `π` — never anything else.  This is the whole\nreason a flat tetrahedron has zero volume: `Λ` vanishes at both. ","signatureChunk":0}]}